From 250c3a2e175552c6d0ccbbfbf6ce887ffee2fe44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] HP: port to BioSTEAM 2.54 / thermosteam 0.54 / pandas 3

- units.py: import StirredTankReactor from abstract_stirred_tank_reactor when
  no longer exported by biosteam.units; pass V_max (renamed from V) to
  BatchBioreactor._init; disable stream linking for HPStorageTank (thermosteam
  0.54 Stream.copy_like on a linked outlet empties a two-phase MultiStream inlet,
  zeroing the acrylic acid product on first simulation).
- _adsorption_column_TSA.py: vendor AdsorptionColumnTSA from BioSTEAM 2.49.2
  (removed in 2.49.3) so the separation design/cost assumptions are unchanged;
  process_areas.py uses it.
- process_areas.py: positional Series indexing via .iloc (pandas 3).
- utils.py/systems: get_TEA_breakdown_df works around read-only
  DataFrame.values in bst.UnitGroup.df_from_groups under pandas 3.
- cellulosic create_facilities: FireWaterTank has no inlets in newer BioSTEAM;
  size it via fire_water_flow_rate (same 0.08 x feedstock basis).

No process assumptions or values changed.

